---- MODULE auditcontract ----
\* Generated by `spk compile` from spec `audit.contract` — source of truth is the
\* spec file; edit there, not here. Extends nothing: the module is
\* self-contained so any engine can open it.

\* No executable invariant fragments (Revision 15).

\* Each State becomes a value in the state variable's range.
StateValues == {"loaded", "verified", "drifted", "refused"}

VARIABLES vpc   \* the state variable (program counter)

vars == <<vpc>>

TypeOK == vpc \in StateValues

\* Initial state: first listed in the spec (the format has no explicit initial marker).
Init == vpc = "loaded"

Next ==
  \* verify_clean: loaded -> verified (guard: [[audit.contract.ac_roundtrip]])
  \/ vpc = "loaded" /\ vpc' = "verified"
  \* verify_drift: loaded -> drifted (guard: [[audit.contract.ac_named_drift]])
  \/ vpc = "loaded" /\ vpc' = "drifted"
  \* refuse_profile: loaded -> refused (guard: [[audit.contract.ac_profile_match]])
  \/ vpc = "loaded" /\ vpc' = "refused"
  \* reverify: drifted -> drifted (guard: [[audit.contract.ac_deterministic]])
  \/ vpc = "drifted" /\ vpc' = "drifted"
  \* stuttering: guards are prose (uninterpreted) — a terminal
  \* state must not read as an engine-side deadlock
  \/ UNCHANGED vpc

\* No state carries an `emits` field — Output is simply empty.
Output == << >>

